":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":12,"created_at":"2025-05-25T22:40:05Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T19:48:14Z","closed_at":"2025-05-26T22:16:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: Godot Engine v4.4.1.stable.fedora (Official Fedora Linux Repo package.)\nResolved in: Godot Engine v4.4.1 stable flatpak version\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Fedora Linux 42 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon R9 390 Series (radeonsi, hawaii, ACO, DRM 3.61, 6.14.6-300.fc42.x86_64) - AMD Ryzen 5 2600 Six-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen editing existing or new Godot Engine 4.4.1 projects the error appears in the output and the Godot Engine app is forced into Compatibility Mode with an Overridden state so that it cannot be changed.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. install Fedora Linux Official repo Godot Engine 4.4.1 stable package\n2. start Godot Engine\n3. select an existing project and click edit or create a new project  and edit it.\n4. The project will open in \"Compatibility (Overridden)\" mode. Unable to change to any other mode.\n5. The following errors will appear in the output:\n  ERROR: Required extension VK_KHR_surface not found.\n  ERROR: drivers/vulkan/rendering_context_driver_vulkan.cpp:928 - Condition \"err != OK\" is true. Returning: err\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com